  "worked_solution": "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the rotation, $Q$ be the matrix that represents the stretching, and $R$ be the matrix that represents the reflection. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nHence, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $RQP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RQP & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n$a+b=(-3)+1=-2.$",
